// stdlib/native/io — platform I/O binding (ADR 0003, layer L2).
//
// SCAFFOLD ONLY. This file declares the intended `io` native surface. It is not
// yet imported by the compiler: the API list currently lives in
// `stdlib/native/manifest.kl` (L1), and `using io;` is still resolved by the
// compiler's native-namespace handling. Once `extern native` lands in the
// parser/checker (ADR 0003 Phase A.3/A.4), this file becomes the importable
// source of truth and the manifest is generated from it.
//
// Intended declarations (syntax TBD, semantics fixed by ADR 0003):
//
//   extern native namespace io {
//     void out(...);      // stdout, printf-style {} formatting
//     void outln(...);    // stdout + newline
//     void err(...);      // stderr
//     void errln(...);    // stderr + newline
//     string in();        // read a line from stdin
//   }
